        "original_id": "2a510aec-94e2-5904-853e-e595bc135d87",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Grandtheft, Aaron Waisglass, Rihanna\n- Roles: DJ, musician, trap artist, singer\n- Places: Toronto, Canada, Barbados\n- Songs: “Summer”, “Sweet Nothing”, “Bitch Better Have My Money”\n- Topics: remixes, digital music releases, chart recognition\n\nFacts:\n- Aaron Waisglass, better known as Grandtheft, is a Canadian DJ and musician based in Toronto.\n- Grandtheft gained recognition as a trap artist for remixing songs such as “Summer,” “Sweet Nothing,” and “Bitch Better Have My Money,” and for having songs chart around the world.\n- Rihanna is a Barbadian singer who recorded the song “Bitch Better Have My Money.”\n- “Bitch Better Have My Money” was digitally released through the iTunes Store on March 26, 2015.",
